  "name": "present-state",
  "title": "Present-state theory (Mallavarapu and Percy)",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Mallavarapu and Percy's no-go theorem: if a system's present state and inputs fix its future, and consciousness makes a difference, then consciousness cannot depend on the process that produced the state. It must depend only on the present state: \"Consciousness is due not to what a system has done, but what it is.\"",
